<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruscino</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Château-Roussillon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruscino was an ancient settlement at Château-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a>, just east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perpignan">Perpignan</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and the chief town of the Sordones. An oppidum from the 6th century BCE, it was where Gallic chiefs met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> in 218 BCE, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>, and later became a Roman town with a forum. It declined in late antiquity but gave its name to the region of Roussillon.</p></div>
